o saved the child from under the wheel and got hurt himself?\" [2250] \"That's the one. He had no identification and no one came to claim him. It looks like he was wanted by the police. He never regained consciousness and died last night. But his identity was established. He was a deserter named Ronald Hammers, who served as a captain in South Lom County.\" [2251] \"Phyllis Hyde's husband?\" [2252] \"Yes. He had an old ticket to Chipping Craighorne and, by the way, a lot of money.\" [2253] \"So he did get money from his wife. I always thought he was the one talking to Phyllis in the gazebo. Of course, she denied it. Sir, the accident happened before\u2014\"\n[2254] Ridestad interrupted him:\n[2255] \"Yes. He was admitted to Milchester General Hospital on the 28th, and the robbery at the small farm took place on the 29th. This rules out any possibility of his being involved in the incident. However, his wife, of course, doesn't know about the accident. She's keeping quiet, which is natural, as he is her husband.\" [2256] \"Truly a heroic act of bravery, isn't it, sir?\" Corradino said slowly. [2257] \"Saving a child from under the wheels? Yeah, that's something. Don't think Hammers fled from the army out of cowardice. But that's all in the past now. For a man who ruined his own reputation, it's a fitting end.\" [2258] \"I am happy for her,\" said the Inspector, \"and for their son as well.\" [2259] \"Yes, he need not feel too ashamed of his father. The young woman can remarry again.\" [2260] Kordok slowly said, \"I was also thinking about this, Director... this shows... possibilities.\" [2261] \"Since you were on the scene, it would be best for you to deliver the news.\u201d\n[2262] \"I will, Chief. I'll go right away. Perhaps it would be best to wait until she returns to the small enclosure. The news might be quite shocking, and besides, I'd like to talk to someone else first.\" [2263] ** ** **\n[2264] [1] Charlotte's first letter is C.\n[2265] Chapter Nineteen: Recap of the Case\n[2266] 1\n[2267] \"I'll get a lamp and put it on the side for you, and then I'll leave,\" said Round Round. \"It's quite dark here. I think a storm is coming.\" [2268] She picked up the small reading lamp and put it on the other side of the table, so that the light would shine on Miss Marple as she knitted her sweater. She was sitting in a large high-backed chair. [2269] The wire was run across the table, and the cat leaped up onto the table and began biting and clawing at the wire. [2270] \"Don't move, Tigris, don't\u2026 It's terrible. Look, it's almost bitten through the wire, it's all broken. Don't you know? You silly little cat, you'll get electrocuted if you do that.\" [2271] \"Thank you, dear,\" said Miss Maple, reaching out to turn on the light. [2272] \"Not that one. You have to press the small switch in the middle of the wire. Wait a moment, I'll take these flowers away so they don't get in the way.\" [2273] She picked up a bottle of Christmas roses from the other end of the table. Tiggy wagged his tail and suddenly extended a mischievous paw, scratching Yuan Yuan's arm. She splashed some water from the vase onto the wires that Tiggy had bitten and onto Tiggy himself, who growled angrily and jumped off the table. [2274] Miss Maple pressed the small pear-shaped switch. A spark burst from the spot where the wires had been bitten and wet with water. [2275] \"Oh, dear,\" said Yuan Yuan. \"The fuse has blown. Now I guess all the lights should be off. \" She tried each switch. \"Yes, they're all off. So, all the lines are connected to this small device, how stupid. And it's burned a spot on the table. It's all Tiggy's fault, the mischievous one. Auntie Jane, what's wrong? Are you scared?\" [2276] \"No, dear. I just happened to notice something I should have seen before\u2026\"\n[2277] \"I'll go change the fuse and then bring the table lamp from Julian's study.\" [2278] \"No, dear, don't bother. You'll miss your bus. I don't need the light anymore